# NOTE: one pattern per line. The original version of this file had
# "dist/ build/ .vite/ coverage/" on a single line, which git reads as one
# literal path containing spaces — so none of those directories were actually
# ignored, and `coverage/` turned up staged on the first real commit.

node_modules/

# Build and tool output
dist/
build/
dist-types/
.vite/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Convex codegen output is COMMITTED, deliberately — do not add it back here.
#
# `apps/web/src/data/store.tsx` imports `convex/_generated/api`, and the CLI's
# own help says it plainly: "This code is generated automatically while running
# `npx convex dev` and should be committed to the repo (your code won't
# typecheck without it!)". Ignoring it meant a fresh clone and every CI run
# failed until someone ran `npx convex dev` — which needs a browser login and a
# live deployment, neither of which CI has.
#
# Regenerate with `npm run convex:codegen` after changing the schema or any
# function signature, and commit the result alongside the change that caused it.

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.convex/
*.pem
*.key

.DS_Store
